  "interpretation": [
    "Original baseline summary-pass and selected predicates were insufficient for the explicit trace-isolation requirement: the erased fixture retained PASS summaries and produced baseline read admission plus a SQL joint row, while the candidate rejected the missing required field.",
    "After the single-list insertion, the intact positive remains admitted by both adapters; the erased fixture is rejected by both, the baseline marks the required field missing/UNAVAILABLE, and its SQL joint count becomes zero.",
    "The baseline_fact_projection certificates in the harness are newly generated semantic projections of baseline outputs. They are not certificates natively produced by the SQL baseline.",
    "All supplied semantic certificates pass the checker, including the original baseline mistaken admission. This demonstrates conditional checking of admitted facts, not independent authentication of the erased external premise.",
    "The retained semantic scope label is historical library metadata; each actual certificate snapshot binds the new plan, full derived-fixture descriptor and baseline-code digest. Original internal run identity remains unchanged."
  ],
